From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:46:43 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] segacd-carts

A Sega CD game stands on the shelf as a jewel case with its disc inside,
drawn by the PlayStation case renderer (ADR 0069) at the same size,
with the same neutrals, cover well, tray and insert animation, so a
Sega CD case and a PS1 case with the same cover are the same pixels.
Japanese discs get the spine card (obi) the JP style draws. North
American Sega CD games shipped in larger cases about the size of a VHS
keep case; v1 draws the jewel case for them too, the cover fitted whole
in the square well, and leaves that case as a deferred style. The style comes from the file name
tags, then the region byte at 0x20b of a .cue or .iso, then USA, the
same order as the BIOS check; a set of two or more discs is the double
case. The cover is Labels/SEGACD/<stem>.png and the disc scan
Labels/SEGACD/disc/<stem>.png, printed outside the hub as on PS1.
